! Band structure of the si2-nc-pbe density, along the same path QE's own
! pw_scf/scf-1.in uses.
!
! A 'bands' run is not self-contained: it reads the density a previous scf run
! left behind, so this case is generated in the same directory as si2-nc-pbe
! immediately after it (see tools/generate_reference.py). That is exactly the
! situation run_bands is in -- a converged density, a frozen potential, one
! diagonalisation per k-point -- and what it checks here is that the potential
! rebuilt from that density carries the gradient correction. Without it the
! bands come out shifted by tenths of an eV while everything still converges.
 &control
    calculation = 'bands'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=2, celldm(1)=10.20, nat=2, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=20.0
    nbnd=8
 /
 &electrons
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pbe-rrkj.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS tpiba_b
  5
  0.00  0.00  0.00 5
  1.00  0.00  0.00 5
  1.00  0.25  0.25 5
  0.50  0.50  0.50 5
  0.00  0.00  0.00 1
